# var-lib-rancher-k3s-server-db.mount — back the k3s kine/SQLite datastore
# (state.db + its WAL, ~110 MB live) with tmpfs, so control-plane fsyncs are
# RAM-speed and can never queue behind CI churn on the array, and so the
# reconstruct-on-boot path is EXERCISED on every reboot and cannot rot.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS: livespec plan ci-runner-pod-lifecycle-reliability,
# research/003 — under 60+ concurrent CI jobs the array saturated, kine
# logged `Slow SQL`, Kueue lost its leader lease and exited, its single
# admission webhook dropped, and every pod creation in the fleet failed.
# Putting the datastore in RAM removes it from that contention entirely.
#
# VOLATILITY IS THE POINT — AND IS SAFE ONLY BECAUSE OF TWO SIBLING UNITS.
# tmpfs is cleared on REBOOT (it survives a plain `systemctl restart k3s`).
# On every boot k3s therefore starts with an EMPTY datastore, and the
# cluster is rebuilt from this repository by, in order:
#   1. inject-github-app-secret.service  (livespec-qqzlek — the GitHub App
#      secret, decrypted from the host credstore)
#   2. converge-ci-stack.service         (livespec-olp4c5 — ARC + every
#      scale set + Kueue + every queue)
# Both are WantedBy=multi-user.target and After=k3s.service. Do NOT enable
# this mount on a host where those two are not installed, enabled and
# proven — it would boot into an empty cluster nothing rebuilds.
# (install-datastore-tmpfs.sh pre-gates on exactly that.)
#
# SAFETY PROPERTIES, deliberately chosen:
#   - Ordered Before=k3s.service, but k3s is NOT made to Require it. If this
#     mount ever fails, k3s starts on the ON-DISK datastore underneath — a
#     safe, degraded fallback (stale but intact), never a blocked boot.
#   - The tmpfs is mounted OVER the on-disk directory: it hides the disk
#     copy, it does not delete it. ROLLBACK is: stop k3s, disable + stop
#     this mount, start k3s — back on the original datastore, untouched.
#   - A reboot clears the datastore AND every container together, so the
#     API's view and the running containers are never out of step (no
#     split-brain). No snapshot/restore leg is provided: restoring a stale
#     datastore into a live cluster would be actively harmful.
#   - size= is a ceiling, not a reservation — tmpfs consumes RAM only as
#     written. mode=0700 preserves the on-disk directory's root-only perms.
#     noexec/nosuid/nodev: a SQLite directory needs none of them.
#
# INSTALL with install-datastore-tmpfs.sh, which ENABLES for next boot and
# NEVER starts this live — starting it under a RUNNING k3s would hide its
# datastore mid-flight. Activation is a boot, or a deliberate cutover with
# k3s stopped.
[Unit]
Description=tmpfs for the k3s kine/SQLite datastore (volatile; cluster reconstructed on boot)
Before=k3s.service

[Mount]
What=tmpfs
Where=/var/lib/rancher/k3s/server/db
Type=tmpfs
Options=size=2G,mode=0700,noexec,nosuid,nodev

[Install]
WantedBy=multi-user.target
